<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">blessings</ansi>

Blessings are small perks that follow your account. When a character of
yours does something worth remembering, the deed is written in their
chronicle (<ansi fg="command">help chronicle</ansi>), and some deeds unlock a blessing. Your <ansi fg="yellow">next</ansi>
characters start with it, even after you delete the one who earned it
(<ansi fg="command">help delete</ansi>).

<ansi fg="command">blessings</ansi> lists what your character carries, what you have earned that waits
for your next character, and what is still to earn, with your progress.
In the web client, the Character window's Overview shows the same.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What they give</ansi>

A blessing gives one of two things, and never combat power beyond a
starting item:

  - A <ansi fg="yellow">starting item</ansi> in the pack: a camp supply such as a flask of broth, a
    warming draught, a cooling salve or sigil chalk. Markets never buy
    these back, so a blessing is not a way to make gold.
  - A <ansi fg="yellow">recruit discount</ansi>: a few percent off what a recruiter asks
    (<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). All of a character's discounts together never come to
    more than 10%.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How they are earned</ansi>

  - From the lifetime counts in the chronicle: a boss slain, relics found,
    companions taken on, beaten foes spared, scenes seen through, a class
    promotion. The counts are of one character's chronicle.
  - <ansi fg="itemname">Iron</ansi> blessings count only the deeds of an Iron character
    (<ansi fg="command">help hardcore</ansi>).
  - You are told the moment one is earned. It is yours for good, once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When they are given</ansi>

At the end of character creation, once. A character keeps the blessings it
was given, and a blessing earned later by that same character waits for the
next one. Characters made before blessings existed carry none, but what they
earn from now on reaches their successors.

Nothing here moves the world's clock, or makes any fight easier or harder.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help chronicle</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hardcore</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help delete</ansi>.
